---
layout: layouts/base.njk
description: "Handmade solid wood kitchens, cabinetry, staircases, windows and doors, designed, made and fitted by cabinet maker Joel Dyter from his workshop in Hebden Bridge, West Yorkshire."
bodyClass: page-home
---
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container hero__grid">
    <div class="hero__text">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cabinet maker · Hebden Bridge</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">Bespoke handmade kitchens, <em>built around the way you live.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Every kitchen is drawn, made and fitted by Joel Dyter, a joiner and cabinet maker with more than {{ site.yearsTrade }} years' experience. The same care goes into his furniture, staircases, windows and doors, and many of his projects can be followed here from the first sketch to the finished room.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start your project</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/projects/">See recent work</a>
      </div>
      <a class="hero__wa" href="{{ site.whatsapp | whatsappHref(site.whatsappMessage) }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ icon("whatsapp", 18) }} Quick question? WhatsApp Joel</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__media">
      {% image "/images/projects/charcoal-shaker-kitchen/03.jpg", "Charcoal Shaker kitchen with an oak-topped island, handmade by Joel Dyter", "(min-width: 900px) 50vw, 100vw", "", "eager" %}
      <p class="hero__tag">Charcoal Shaker kitchen · <a href="/projects/charcoal-shaker-kitchen/">see how it was made</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="container">
    <ul class="trust">
      <li><strong>{{ site.yearsTrade }}+ years</strong> as a joiner and cabinet maker</li>
      <li><strong>Own workshop</strong> since {{ site.established }}</li>
      <li><strong>Designed, made</strong> and fitted by Joel</li>
      <li><strong>Solid timber</strong> with hand-cut joints</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Bespoke work</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Made to measure, for every room in the house</h2>
        <p class="section-head__intro">Every piece is designed and made for its space, using solid timber chosen to suit the room.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="tiles">
      {%- set tileImages = {
        "kitchens": ["/images/projects/holland-kitchen-heptonstall/01.jpg", "Painted cottage kitchen in Heptonstall"],
        "bathrooms": ["/images/projects/washroom/01.jpg", "Painted washroom cabinetry"],
        "cabinetry": ["/images/projects/under-stairs-storage/01.jpg", "Painted under-stairs cupboards"],
        "furniture": ["/images/projects/farmhouse-dining-table/01.jpg", "Farmhouse dining table"],
        "staircases": ["/images/projects/staircases/05.jpg", "Winding oak staircase"],
        "windows-and-doors": ["/images/projects/oak-front-door/01.jpg", "Oak door in a stone arch"]
      } %}
      {%- asyncEach s in services %}
      <li class="tile">
        <a href="/{{ s.slug }}/">
          <div class="tile__media">{% image tileImages[s.slug][0], tileImages[s.slug][1], "(min-width: 1100px) 30vw, (min-width: 640px) 45vw, 92vw" %}</div>
          <h3 class="tile__title">{{ s.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ s.blurb }}</p>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endeach %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="split__media">{% image "/images/site/dovetail-drawer.jpg", "Hand-cut dovetails on a solid timber drawer", "(min-width: 900px) 45vw, 100vw" %}</div>
    <div class="split__text prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">How Joel works</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Fewer projects, each given the time it deserves</h2>
      <figure class="pull-quote">
        <blockquote><p>“I would rather do fewer jobs than hurry any of them.”</p></blockquote>
        <figcaption>Joel Dyter</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>Joel takes on only a few projects at a time, so each one gets his full attention, from the first drawing to the final fitting. Timber is chosen with care, joints are cut by hand, and every piece is given the time it needs to be made properly, so it wears in rather than wears out.</p>
      <p>He has worked as a joiner and cabinet maker for more than {{ site.yearsTrade }} years, and has run his own workshop in the Calder Valley since {{ site.established }}. Because he designs, makes and fits everything himself, the person who listens to your ideas at the start is the same person who fits the last cupboard to your wall.</p>
      <p>Many homes here have uneven stone walls and old flagged floors. Taking the time to scribe each piece to them is what makes it look as though it has always been there.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">More about Joel and the process, start to finish {{ icon("arrow", 16) }}</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Portfolio</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Kitchens, staircases and furniture from the workshop</h2>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/projects/">See all projects</a>
    </div>
    <div class="cards">
      {%- asyncEach p in collections.projects | featured | limit(6) %}{% include "partials/project-card.njk" %}{% endeach %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--dark">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">The process</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">From first conversation to final fitting</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><h3>Conversation</h3><p>Get in touch by phone, WhatsApp or the enquiry form to talk through what you have in mind.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Photos &amp; site visit</h3><p>A few photos give Joel a first idea of the room. He then visits to measure up and see how you use the space.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Estimate</h3><p>An early estimate gives you a sense of the cost before any detailed design work begins.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Drawings</h3><p>Joel draws up the design, so you can see how each piece will look and fit the room.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Final price &amp; agreement</h3><p>Once the design is settled, the build price is agreed. Changes requested mid-build, and the cost of fitting, may vary depending on the work involved.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Made by hand</h3><p>Cabinets and furniture are made by hand in the Hebden Bridge workshop.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Fitting</h3><p>Joel fits each piece himself, scribing it to your walls and floors so it sits neatly in the room.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

